r.theorem-5.6"],"id":"euler.theorem-5.6","kind":"claim","label":"Theorem 5.6","locator":"Theorem 5.6, Section 5","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Theorem 5.6.** There is an absolute exponent $C$ such that the following holds if $\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-1/12}\\le1$. For all integers $n\\ge0$ and $p\\ge2$, the construction satisfies $$\\begin{align}\n \\|V_p\\|_{[n],\\gamma}+\\|f_p+f_p^S\\|_{[n],\\gamma}\n        +\\lambda\\|\\mathsf p_p\\|_{[n],\\gamma}\n &\\le C_{n,p}\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-5/4}\\lambda^{-2(p-1)/3}, \\tag{5.34}\\\\\n \\|B_p\\|_{[n]}+\\|\\bar f_p\\|_{[n]}\n &\\le C_{n,p}\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-5/2}\\lambda^{-2(p-2)/3}, \\tag{5.35}\\\\\n \\|C_{p+1}\\|_{[n],\\gamma}\n &\\le C_{n,p}\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-9/4}\\lambda^{-2(p-1)/3}. \\tag{5.36}\n\\end{align}$$ The bounds (5.34) and (5.36) also hold for $p=1$, with $f_1=f_1^S=0$. For all integers $P\\ge2$ and $m\\ge0$, the expansion of Proposition 5.4 at the depth $P$ satisfies $$\\begin{equation}\n \\|W_{\\rm osc}\\|_{[m],\\gamma}\\le C_{m,P}\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-5/4},\\qquad\n \\Big\\|\\sum_{p=2}^PB_p\\Big\\|_{[m]}+\\Big\\|\\sum_{p=2}^P\\bar f_p\\Big\\|_{[m]}\n \\le C_{m,P}\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{-5/2}, \\tag{5.37}\n\\end{equation}$$ and its remainder satisfies $$\\begin{equation}\n \\|R_P\\|_{[m]}\\le C_{m,P}\\lambda^{-5/4}\\lambda^{-2P/3}. \\tag{5.38}\n\\end{equation}$$","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.theorem-5.6","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-5.10","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.10%22%2C%22euler.theorem-5.6%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.10%22%2C%22euler.theorem-5.6%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curate